node_modules/
# data/ holds build artefacts and is rebuilt every deploy - with one
# exception. The room-assignment override is a committed SOURCE file: it is
# the correction we cannot make in the read-only registry workbook, and
# Netlify and the daily workflow have no other way to see it. Written as
# data/* rather than data/ so git descends into the directory and the
# negation below can take effect. See fetch.js loadRoomOverrides().
data/*
!data/room-overrides.json
dist/
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json

.env.local
